50,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"The candidates are A, B, C, and D. Given the data, I find the Microbiome Atlas, D, appealing for its catalogue nature.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"I disagree. D requires field sites and phenotyping. I prefer C, Protein Folding Dynamics, as it relies on simulation.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"C is risky because of the spectroscopy suite's instability. I lean toward A, Plant Drought Signaling, as it uses glasshouses.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,A is problematic because glasshouses are booked solid. C is the most cost-effective due to the computing agreement.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Midori,,"A is indoor, but the booking issue is real. D is too risky with the field sites. I think C is the most viable.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Victoria, if the glasshouses are full, A cannot proceed. Perhaps C is the most pragmatic choice despite the equipment.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Benjamin, you mentioned the computing agreement. If the analysts are seconded, can C actually be completed?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"The analysts are gone until autumn, but the project is multi-year. The simulation part can wait or be outsourced.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,True. The immediate cost savings on computing outweigh the temporary staffing gap in my view.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Midori,,I agree. C seems to avoid the most critical bottlenecks we've identified.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"I am swayed. The longevity of catalogue work is great, but the immediate risks to D are too high. I will support C.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,I am satisfied with C. It aligns with the current staffing trends and the computing budget.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"I still worry about the spectroscopy, but compared to the glasshouse backlog, C is the better option.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,It seems we have a consensus. C is the most rational choice given the current infrastructure and costs.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Midori,,I agree. Let us move to the vote.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
